-- title:
--   Reducedness of k[[X₀,X₁]]/(f) for a Drinfeld-type crossing
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $k$ be a field in which $q = 0$, i.e. $(q : k) = 0$. Let $f$ be a formal power series in two variables over $k$, an element of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k`, whose variables are written $X_0 =$ `X 0` and $X_1 =$ `X 1`. Assume that $f$ agrees with the form $X_0 X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q} X_1$ up to terms of order at least $q+2$, in the precise sense that the difference $f - (X_0 X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q} X_1)$ lies in the $(q+2)$-nd power of the ideal of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k` generated by $X_0$ and $X_1$. The conclusion is that the quotient ring $k[[X_0,X_1]]/(f)$, formed as the quotient of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k` by the principal ideal `Ideal.span {f}`, is reduced: it has no nonzero nilpotent elements. No hypothesis of completeness, separability or perfectness on $k$ is imposed beyond $(q:k)=0$, and $f$ itself is not assumed to be anything more than congruent to the displayed form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$.
--
--   The ring $k[[X_0,X_1]]/(f)$ with $f \equiv X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1 \bmod (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ is the local model, in characteristic $q$, of the crossing of the $q+1$ branches indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$ that occurs on the Drinfeld-level modular curves; the leading form is the product $\prod_{[a:b] \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)}(bX_0 - aX_1)$ of $q+1$ pairwise non-proportional linear forms. This reducedness statement is used in the variant over a residue field after base change, [`MvPowerSeries.isReduced_residueField_tensorProduct_quotient_span_C_mul_sub_mul_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.isReduced_residueField_tensorProduct_quotient_span_C_mul_sub_mul_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow), in the analysis of the special fibre of the relevant local models.
-- source:
